{"shortDescription":"By Jeslyn LerhMarine fuel sales in Singapore edged higher for a fourth consecutive month in August on the back of resilient demand, official data showed on Monday.Bunker activity held steady to firmer at the world's largest vessel refuelling hub by volume, with the market working around earlier sup…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["By Jeslyn Lerh"]},{"type":"p","children":["Marine fuel sales in Singapore edged higher for a fourth consecutive month in August on the back of resilient demand, official data showed on Monday."]},{"type":"p","children":["Bunker activity held steady to firmer at the world's largest vessel refuelling hub by volume, with the market working around earlier supply concerns, industry sources said."]},{"type":"p","children":["Bunker sales totalled 4.77 million metric tons in August, up 0.7% month on month, though down 3.9% year on year, data from the Maritime and Port Authority of Singapore showed."]},{"type":"p","children":["Demand for high-sulphur marine fuels retained strong momentum, with volumes up 7.3% from July to 2.10 million tons in August. In contrast, low-sulphur fuel bunker volumes eased by 5.8% month on month to 2.19 million tons."]},{"type":"p","children":["Total marine gasoil sales extended gains, hitting a six-month high of 367,700 tons."]},{"type":"p","children":["Conventional fuels continued to make up the bulk of the bunkering market share, with alternative fuels comprising only 2% to 2.5% of total volumes."]},{"type":"p","children":["Bio-blended bunker sales rebounded by 45.1% month on month to 57,300 tons but softened by 57.6% from August last year."]},{"type":"p","children":["Meanwhile, liquefied natural gas bunker sales held largely stable from the previous month, totalling 58,600 tons in August, while sliding 12.4% year on year."]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[]},{"